Dave's right, it just opens you up to too much chance.  Instead of
poison or /Death being the YAADs early on, all of a sudden every attack
wand (cold/fire/lightning/magic missile/etc), or pit, or chest trap, or
whatever can kill you instantly--as can any fast monster that corners
you.  Soon after Sokoban you'll have enough gold to get some decent
protection anyway.

Basically, you're making the first 6-8 levels you play _much_ more
risky, in exchange for making the next 6-8 _slightly_ easier, and after
that point you'll be in the same position either way.  A very bad
tradeoff, IMO.

Now, buffing up the pet is a decent thing to do, let it eat all those
gnomes once you're high enough level that their XP isn't worthwile.



